    {
      "_id": "6aeaeeac1154a1055518c252",
      "title": "갑자기 모두가 듣고 싶어 하는 하버드의 혹독한 수업",
      "message": "<article class=\"nv-text\">\n<p class=\"nv-cover\"><img class=\"nv-cover-img\" src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2ThTdQFo2uM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"갑자기 모두가 듣고 싶어 하는 하버드의 혹독한 수업\" loading=\"eager\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"></p>\n<div class=\"nv-lead\">\n<p class=\"nv-lead-text\">갑자기 모두가 듣고 싶어 하는 하버드의 혹독한 수업 주제를 다룬 The Wall Street Journal 기사에서 주요 시사 영단어를 정리합니다. *AI 음성과 이미지를 사용했습니다.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"nv-body\">\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">an ungodly amount of reading (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">ungodly</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">엄청난 양의 독서</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. ungodly: 터무니없이 많은, 엄청난 (형) ※ 원래 “신을 따르지 않는, 불경한”(un+godly) → “말도 안 되게 많은, 지독한”</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">So why are freshmen lining up to get into Humanities 10? (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">humanities</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">그렇다면 왜 신입생들은 ‘인문학 10’을 들으려고 줄을 서는 걸까?</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. humanities: 인문학 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">Samantha Matherne paced as she marked up on a white board... (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">pace</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">사만다 매서른은 화이트보드에 필기하며 왔다 갔다 했다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. pace: 서성거리다, 왔다 갔다 하다 (동)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">with segues into Adam Smith and Immanuel Kant (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">segue</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">애덤 스미스와 이마누엘 칸트 이야기로 자연스럽게 넘어가며</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. segue: 자연스러운 전환 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">It's a fever that even the professors are struggling to explain. (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">fever</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">교수들조차 설명하기 어려워하는 열풍이다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. fever: 열풍, 열기 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">The class is definitely not for padding the GPA. (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">pad</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">이 수업은 분명 평균 학점을 손쉽게 높이기 위한 수업이 아니다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. pad: 부풀리다, (날조하여) 덧붙이다 (동)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">Students read a hefty book a week (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">hefty</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">학생들은 매주 두툼한 책 한 권을 읽는다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. hefty: 많은, 두둑한, 분량이 상당한 (형)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">Digital devices are verboten (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">verboten</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">디지털 기기는 금지된다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. verboten: 금지된 (형)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;Western Civ,&quot; &quot;Great Books&quot; and &quot;the canon&quot; (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">canon</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">‘서양 문명’, ‘위대한 저서들’, 그리고 ‘정전’</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. canon: 주요 문헌[작품] 목록, (음악의) 캐논 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">the need to combat frayed attention spans (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">frayed</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">약해진 집중력에 맞서야 할 필요성</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. frayed: 닳고 약해진, 흐트러진 (형)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">Several mentioned with disdain (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">disdain</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">몇몇은 경멸하는 태도로 언급했다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. disdain: 경멸, 업신여김 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">Hum 10 was conceived as a Harvard twist (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">conceive</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">Hum 10은 하버드식 변형으로 구상되었다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. conceive: 구상하다, 고안하다 (동)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">Harvard's loftiest faculty members (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">lofty</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">하버드에서 가장 명망 높은 교수들</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. lofty: 지위나 명성이 높은 (형)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">exposure to first-years is a tonic (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">tonic</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">신입생들을 접하는 것은 활력소다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. tonic: 활력을 주는 것, 활력소 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">their enthusiasm and the newness of it all (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">newness</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">그들의 열정과 그 모든 것의 새로움</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. newness: 새로움 (명)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">students seemed to especially relish debating their classmates (<mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">relish</mark>)</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">학생들은 특히 급우들과 토론하는 것을 즐기는 듯했다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. relish: 크게 즐기다, 만끽하다 (동)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n</div>\n<footer class=\"nv-related-links\">\n<p class=\"nv-related-link-line\"><a class=\"nv-related-link nv-related-link--youtube\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ThTdQFo2uM\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">📺</span> 유튜브 보기</a></p>\n<div class=\"board-comments-root nv-related-comments\" data-board-comments-root></div>\n</footer>\n<footer class=\"nv-source\">\n  <p class=\"nv-source-label\">출처</p>\n  <p class=\"nv-source-text\">The Wall Street Journal | The Brutal Harvard Class That Suddenly Everyone Wants to Take | By Pamela Paul | Oct. 27, 2026</p>\n  <p class=\"nv-source-link-wrap\"><a class=\"nv-source-link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/lifestyle/harvard-class-humanities-32e06366?mod=WSJ_home_feature_6_pos_3\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">원문 기사 보기</a></p>\n</footer>\n</article>",
      "slug": "ungodly-humanities-pace-segue-fever-related-words",
      "metaDescription": "The Wall Street Journal 기사에서 추출한 시사 영단어. ungodly, humanities, pace, segue, fever, pad, hefty, verboten, canon, frayed, disdain, conceive, lofty, tonic, newness, relish.",
      "date": "2026-10-27",
