    {
      "_id": "6aec84565cfe0b3c2f6f07de",
      "title": "민주당의 놀라운 승리",
      "message": "<article class=\"nv-text\">\n<p class=\"nv-cover\"><img class=\"nv-cover-img\" src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WBhplbUQAS0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"민주당의 놀라운 승리\" loading=\"eager\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"></p>\n<div class=\"nv-lead\">\n<p class=\"nv-lead-text\">민주당의 놀라운 승리 주제를 다룬 The Economist 기사에서 주요 시사 영단어를 정리합니다. *AI 음성과 이미지를 사용했습니다.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"nv-body\">\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;The Democrats’ extraordinary <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">triumph</mark>, explained&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">민주당의 이례적인 대승을 분석하다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. triumph: 대승, 큰 성공 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;Democrats won by <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">landslide</mark> margins in Senate elections in Georgia and North Carolina, too.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">민주당은 조지아주와 노스캐롤라이나주 상원의원 선거에서도 압도적인 표 차이로 승리했다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. landslide: 압승 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;The epicentre of the <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">rout</mark> was in the Republicans’ own backyard—the South.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">참패의 진원지는 공화당의 텃밭인 미국 남부였다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. rout: 참패, 대패 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;The swing was in part a result of <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">turnout</mark> among black voters.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">이러한 표심 변화는 부분적으로 흑인 유권자들의 투표 참여에 따른 결과였다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. turnout: 투표율, 투표 참여 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;Adam Hamilton improved on Kamala Harris’s margins by an eye-popping 52 percentage points.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">애덤 해밀턴은 카멀라 해리스의 득표 격차보다 놀랍게도 52%포인트 개선된 성적을 거뒀다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. margin: 득표율 격차 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;he united much of the country in rebuking his presidency.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">그는 국민 상당수를 자신의 대통령직을 강하게 비판하는 데 하나로 뭉치게 했다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. rebuke: 질책하다, 강하게 비판하다 (동사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;Many voters who once identified with Mr Trump now see his <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">enforcement</mark> regime as cruel and discriminatory.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">과거 트럼프에게 동조했던 많은 유권자는 이제 그의 단속 체제를 잔혹하고 차별적인 것으로 보고 있다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. enforcement: 법 집행, 단속 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;This may be explained in part by the Trump administration’s <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">heavy-handed</mark> approach to immigration.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">이는 부분적으로 트럼프 행정부의 강압적인 이민 정책으로 설명될 수 있다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. heavy-handed: 강압적인, 고압적인 (형용사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;now see his enforcement regime as cruel and <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">discriminatory</mark>.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">이제 그의 단속 체제를 잔혹하고 차별적인 것으로 보고 있다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. discriminatory: 차별적인 (형용사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;The Democrats’ <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">extraordinary</mark> triumph, explained&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">민주당의 이례적인 대승을 분석하다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. extraordinary: 이례적인, 비범한 (형용사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;Adam Hamilton improved on Kamala Harris’s margins by an <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">eye-popping</mark> 52 percentage points.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">애덤 해밀턴은 카멀라 해리스의 득표 격차보다 무려 52%포인트 개선된 성적을 거뒀다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. eye-popping: 눈이 휘둥그레질 만큼 놀라운 (형용사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;The <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">epicentre</mark> of the rout was in the Republicans’ own backyard—the South.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">참패의 진원지는 공화당의 텃밭인 미국 남부였다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. epicentre: 진원지, 중심지 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;In counties where naturalised citizens make up a greater share of the <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">electorate</mark>, the swing was even larger than you would expect from the Hispanic share of the electorate alone.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">귀화 시민이 전체 유권자에서 차지하는 비중이 높은 카운티에서는 히스패닉 유권자 비중만으로 예상되는 것보다 더 큰 표심 이동이 나타났다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. electorate: 유권자 전체 (명사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;In counties where <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">naturalised</mark> citizens make up a greater share of the electorate,&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">귀화 시민이 전체 유권자에서 더 큰 비중을 차지하는 카운티에서는,</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. naturalised: 귀화한 (형용사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n<section class=\"nv-word-section nv-narrative\">\n  <p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-quote nv-ex-en\">&quot;In today’s <mark class=\"nv-hl nv-hl--soft\">polarised</mark> America, it would seem impossible to build a sizeable coalition of voters who agree on anything.&quot;</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-gloss nv-ex-ko\">오늘날처럼 양극화된 미국에서는 어떤 사안에든 의견을 같이하는 상당한 규모의 유권자 연합을 구축하는 것이 불가능해 보인다.</p>\n<p class=\"nv-narrative-text nv-narrative-def\">cf. polarised: 양극화된 (형용사)</p>\n  <hr class=\"nv-section-rule\" />\n</section>\n</div>\n<footer class=\"nv-related-links\">\n<p class=\"nv-related-link-line\"><a class=\"nv-related-link nv-related-link--youtube\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WBhplbUQAS0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">📺</span> 유튜브 보기</a></p>\n<div class=\"board-comments-root nv-related-comments\" data-board-comments-root></div>\n</footer>\n<footer class=\"nv-source\">\n  <p class=\"nv-source-label\">출처</p>\n  <p class=\"nv-source-text\">The Economist | The Democrats’ extraordinary triumph, explained</p>\n  <p class=\"nv-source-link-wrap\"><a class=\"nv-source-link\" href=\"https://www.economist.com/interactive/graphic-detail/2026/11/04/the-democrats-extraordinary-triumph-explained\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">원문 기사 보기</a></p>\n</footer>\n</article>",
